<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">31 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 31 May, from 1223 to 1970.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mongols" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongols.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1223">1223 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">803 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongols rout the Rus and Cumans at the Kalka River</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Mongol expedition under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebe">Jebe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subutai">Subutai</a> crushed the armies of several Rus princes and their Cuman allies. The full Mongol conquest of the Rus lands came fourteen years later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subutai">Subutai</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1293">1293 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">733 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Raden Wijaya's forces defeat the Mongol expedition to Java</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raden-wijaya">Raden Wijaya</a>, who had used the Mongol expedition sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> against his rival, turned on the invaders and won a major victory. The day was later taken as the founding date of the city of Surabaya.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-invasion-of-java">Mongol invasion of Java</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raden-wijaya">Raden Wijaya</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1578">1578 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">448 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Martin Frobisher sails on his third Arctic voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Frobisher left Harwich with fifteen ships to mine what he believed was gold ore on Baffin Island. The ore proved worthless, and the Northwest Passage stayed unfound.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1790">1790 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">236 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington signs the first US copyright law</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Copyright Act protected books, maps and charts for 14 years, renewable once. It drew on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s Statute of Anne and founded American copyright law.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1859">1859 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">167 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Great Clock of Westminster starts keeping time</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The clock in the new tower of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palace-of-westminster">Houses of Parliament</a> began running. Its great bell, Big Ben, struck the hours for the first time that July.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1902">1902 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">124 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Vereeniging ends the South African War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> leaders accepted British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> and Orange Free State in return for promises of self-government. The war had cost tens of thousands of lives, many in British camps.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British and German fleets clash at Jutland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The largest naval battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> lose more ships and men, but the German High Seas Fleet withdrew to port and rarely ventured out again.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1970">1970 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">56 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Earthquake and avalanche devastate northern Peru</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 7.9 earthquake set off an avalanche from Huascarán that buried the town of Yungay. About 70,000 people died, making it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>'s worst natural disaster.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 31 May <span class="n">10</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manuel-i-of-portugal"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manuel-i-of-portugal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manuel I of Portugal</span><span class="tp">1469–1521</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ahilyabai-holkar"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Ahilyabai Holkar</span><span class="tp">1725–1795</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hieronymus-von-colloredo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hieronymus-von-colloredo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hieronymus von Colloredo</span><span class="tp">1732–1812</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hijikata-toshizo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hijikata-toshizo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hijikata Toshizō</span><span class="tp">1835–1869</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-xi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-xi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Pius XI</span><span class="tp">1857–1939</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-younghusband"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-younghusband.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francis Younghusband</span><span class="tp">1863–1942</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rainier-iii-prince-of-monaco"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rainier-iii-prince-of-monaco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rainier III, Prince of Monaco</span><span class="tp">1923–2005</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jim-bolger"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Jim Bolger</span><span class="tp">b. 1935</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dina-boluarte"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dina-boluarte.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Dina Boluarte</span><span class="tp">b. 1962</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/viktor-orban"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/viktor-orban.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Viktor Orbán</span><span class="tp">b. 1963</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 31 May <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/geza-ii-of-hungary"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/geza-ii-of-hungary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Géza II of Hungary</span><span class="tp">1130–1162</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albertino-mussato"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Albertino Mussato</span><span class="tp">1261–1329</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshimitsu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ashikaga-yoshimitsu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ashikaga Yoshimitsu</span><span class="tp">1358–1408</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/martin-of-aragon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/martin-of-aragon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Martin of Aragon</span><span class="tp">1356–1410</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tintoretto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tintoretto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tintoretto</span><span class="tp">1518–1594</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-i-of-prussia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-william-i-of-prussia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick William I of Prussia</span><span class="tp">1688–1740</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joseph-haydn"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joseph-haydn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joseph Haydn</span><span class="tp">1732–1809</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
